{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Lest you make a covenant, etc.</b> That is, even though at the time of making the covenant they would accept upon themselves the seven commandments, nevertheless you shall not make a covenant — and the reason is <b>and they go astray</b>, meaning: the inhabitants of the land follow their elohim, for there is no faithfulness in them, as is plain to one who knows hidden matters — <b>and they sacrifice to their elohim and call you</b>, etc. And they said in tractate Avodah Zarah (Avodah Zarah 8a) that from the moment of the call Scripture accounts it as though he had eaten. And as for the verse saying <b>of his sacrifice</b>, the Rambam wrote in the Laws of Shechitah (chapter 4) that this comes to prohibit the shechitah of a gentile, from the fact that Scripture mentioned them among the prohibitions of gentiles. You thus learn that the dimension of slaughter alone HaShem abominates even though it contains none of the disqualifications of slaughter."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:35.253741139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}